title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › What each chip means
route: /authorizations/eligibility
intro: The coloured chips in the list columns and in the 'Payment checks' rows (in the side panel). Green is fine, amber needs a step, red blocks billing, grey is neutral. A chip always carries a word, never colour alone.
dir: LR
---
start s1 "A coloured chip on the list or the result page"

group gE "Column 'Eligibility'"
  screen e0 "'Eligibility' chip"
  process e1 "'Active' (green)\nThe state or plan says coverage is on for the date of service"
  process e2 "'Lapsed 10/12' (red)\nCoverage dropped on that date. Later days are not payable until it is restored"
  process e3 "'Ended 09/30' (red)\nCoverage ended. The patient may have a new plan: ask the payer"
  process e4 "'Not found' (red)\nNo member matched the ID and date of birth"
  process e5 "'ID differs' (amber)\nCoverage is active, but the plan has the member under another ID"
  process e6 "'Not checked' (grey)\nVerify was paused, so nothing was asked"
endgroup

group gB "Column 'Benefits'"
  screen b0 "'Benefits' chip"
  process b1 "'Covered' (green)\nThe plan pays for this level of care"
  process b2 "'Limited' (amber)\nPaid with conditions: diagnosis on the plan's list, each day authorized"
  process b3 "'Not covered' (red)\nThe plan does not pay for this level of care\nFor example R-1118"
  process b4 "'Not confirmed' (amber)\nThe plan answered for coverage but not for this service\nThe result offers 'Ask Caller to confirm the benefit'"
endgroup

group gA "Column 'Authorization'"
  screen a0 "'Authorization' chip (the day or unit usage is on the quiet second line of the row)"
  process a1 "'Not required' (grey)\nThe payer needs none for this level of care"
  process a2 "'On file' (green)\nApproved. Days or units used so far, such as '9 of 14 days', are on the second line"
  process a3 "'In progress' (grey)\nA request is being drafted"
  process a4 "'Payer reviewing' (grey)\nA request is with the payer"
  process a5 "'Retro request open' (amber)\nA request for days already delivered is open"
  process a6 "'Required, not on file' (amber)\nNeeded before the first day. Not started"
  process a7 "'Requirement unknown' (grey)\nNo rule on file for this payer and level of care. Check with the payer"
endgroup

group gV "Column 'Verdict'"
  screen v0 "'Verdict' chip, right after the patient, with 'Checked 3 h ago' on the quiet second line"
  process v1 "'Cleared to bill' (green)\nEverything passes"
  process v2 "'Authorization first' (amber)\nOnly the authorization is missing"
  process v3 "'Fix before billing' (red)\nCoverage, plan, network, another plan, a limit or the member ID failed,\nor a benefit or enrollment could not be confirmed"
  process v5 "'Not checked' (grey)\nThe check did not run: Verify is paused in Settings"
  process v4 "Second line: 'Checked 3 h ago' or 'Checking now'\nTime since the last check, or a re-check running\n'Re-check due Tue 11:32 am': Verify will run it\n'Re-checked automatically at 11:32 am': it did\n'Not re-checked: Verify is paused in Settings'"
endgroup

goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Which verdict and why"

s1 --> e0 & b0 & a0 & v0
e0 --> e1 & e2 & e3 & e4 & e5 & e6
b0 --> b1 & b2 & b3 & b4
a0 --> a1 & a2 & a3 & a4 & a5 & a6 & a7
v0 --> v1 & v2 & v3 & v4 & v5
v1 & v2 & v3 & v5 --> g1
